just a few weeks after hitting us with  summer game fest and its many world  premieres jeff keeley is back to host  opening night live this event kicks off  the annual european gaming convention  gamescom and jeff has already teased 30  plus games will be shown off opening  night live 2022 will be the first live  in person opening night live  presentation since 2019 following two  years of online only live streams  tickets are available for those  attending gamescom in cologne germany  however for those of us that can't make  the trip to germany there's still an  option to watch it on one of the  expensive screens we all own here's how  gamescom opening night live 2022 will be  available right here on gamespot's  youtube and twitch channel the stream  begins tuesday august 23rd at 11 a.m  pacific time 2 p.m eastern and according  to jeff the stream will run about 2  hours so make sure you have plenty of  snacks and plenty of water you don't  want to be dehydrated when your next  favorite game gets announced previous  opening night lives have also featured  announcements during a half hour  pre-show but at the time of this  recording a similar start has yet to be  confirmed for this year's event however  we will be doing our own pre and post  show to chat about the biggest  announcements and the good news is that  we already know a small list of what you  can expect to see at opening night live  for starters we'll be getting brand new  gameplay for the kalista protocol a new  survival horror game led by dead space  creator glenn schofield so fans of those  games will most definitely love this the  kalista protocol is set in a prison  called black iron located on one of  jupiter's moons callisto protagonist  jacob lee has found himself trapped as  mutated humans begin taking over and  murdering other inmates sounds perfect  for a scaredy cat like me and speaking  of games that i'll probably never play  we'll also get a new look at the outlast  trials another survival horror game that  you can play with up to 4 friends in the  much less scary department we'll be  getting new looks at two games that are  sure to be incredibly hilarious goat  simulator 3 and high on life despite the  number 3 in its title goat sim 3 is  actually the second in the franchise and  the game will once again let you loose  in a sandbox to cause all types of chaos  as a goat meanwhile high on life the  newest title from rick and morty  co-creator justin roiland is an  action-adventure metroidvania  first-person shooter that is by far my  most anticipated out of this confirmed  list jeff also revealed we'll be getting  a new look at the recently delayed  hogwarts legacy as well as the game that  refuses to settle for a delay sonic  frontiers and if you're at gamescom then  you can try out sonic frontiers for  yourself because it's playable at the  show the last two that we know of at the  moment are returned to monkey island and  a brand new sci-fi ip from subnautica  developer unknown worlds entertainment  however i'm sure jeff is going to  continue to tease games as the event  draws closer so make sure to check his  twitter account every now and then if  you want to stay immersed in all things  opening night live and we'll keep a  running list here on gamespot for  comparison's sake last year's opening  night live event included the reveal of  the new saints row and marvel's midnight  suns as well as gameplay for call of  duty vanguard's campaign and death  stranding director's cut leave a comment  with your craziest world premiere  announcement predictions and i might pin  the best one and don't forget to come  back to gamespot on tuesday to watch the  stream  you
 

